# util_est: Utilization Estimation (EWMA)
# Mainline version: 5.0
# Commit: 7f65342d7f25 ("sched/fair: Add util_est")
#
# util_est uses an Exponentially Weighted Moving Average (EWMA) to track
# task utilization, providing a more stable signal for frequency selection
# and Energy Aware Scheduling (EAS) decisions.
#
# Benefits:
#   - Reduces frequency oscillation (tasks ramp up faster, ramp down slower)
#   - Improves EAS task placement decisions
#   - Low overhead (only updated at dequeue time)
#   - CONFIG_SCHED_UTIL_EST_FASTUP: enables faster ramp-up for interactive tasks
#
# Source files (modified):
#   kernel/sched/fair.c       — core util_est implementation
#   kernel/sched/sched.h      — sched_avg structure additions
#   include/linux/sched.h     — sched_entity additions
#   kernel/sched/features.h   — SCHED_FEAT_UTIL_EST feature flag
#
# Backport notes for 4.19:
#   - 4.19's sched_avg structure may differ from 5.0's
#   - WALT (vendor) and PELT can coexist; util_est works with both
#   - ACK 4.19 kernels may already include util_est (check Kconfig)
#   - If SCHED_UTIL_EST exists in Kconfig, no backport needed — just enable it
#
# Config options:
#   CONFIG_SCHED_UTIL_EST=y
#   CONFIG_SCHED_UTIL_EST_FASTUP=y
#
# Risk: Low-Medium (scheduler internal API differences)
# Benefit: Medium (smoother frequency selection, better EAS)
